at reward  is in bitcoins itself which as of today  stands at 12.5 bitcoins  and to add there is no other way that  the bitcoins  can be generated in a bitcoin network it  is only through mining  now the bitcoin network internally  halves the reward  after every 21k blocks which is  approximately every four years so now  subsequently whenever the time period  will end  the mining reward will get reduced to  6.25 btc  now let's take a look at a demo now as i  said  this is a demo to showcase how to  generate a sha-256 hash  using an input value so whatever input i  have the hash which is generated it is  of 256  bytes even if i add a new value  it will again only generate a 256  bit length hash now let's take a look at  a typical  blockchain structure we have a block  over here  which has one transaction added to it  now this is orange in color because it  has not been mined  and i can only add a subsequent block to  it  once it is mined now as this is the  first  block in this particular blockchain the  previous hash value  of this block is all zeros and it is a  called as a genesis block  now as i have mined this block the hash  which is the digital signature of this  block itself has been generated and i  can now  add a block primary thing which to be  noted over here is  that the previous hash value of this new  block is the hash value of the previous  block  it has two transactions aggregated in it  and i can  again mine it and now the hash of this  block has been  generated so this highlights the typical  data structure of a blockchain and how  blocks are linking themselves to each  other now let's take a look of a  typical transaction which happens over a  blockchain now i want to send money from  wallet 1 to wallet 2  and i want to send one dollar there is a  transaction  fee of point one dollar associated with  this transaction now as i have  initiated that transaction wallet one  has been deducted as one point one  dollar and it is a pending transaction  this transaction is waiting to be mined  so i can choose any of the miners to do  this transaction the pending transaction  is  done and now block 2 if you see  has been added the previous hash value  of this block  is 0 0 a 9 is the hash value of block  one  another thing to be noted the value of  the amount in wallet two has also got  incremented by one done again we can try  another transaction  transferring one dollar again from  wallet one  to wallet three and say from wallet 2 to  wallet 3 i have done a transaction it is  pending  it can be mined and block 3 has got  added now what are the key takeaways  today we learned what are the current  issues in the banking system and how  bitcoin solved them what is blockchain  features of blockchain  and the demo of the features which we  have seen i hope you had a great  learning session  and i'll meet you in the next session  thank you  there if you like this video subscribe  to the simply learn youtube channel  and click here to watch similar videos  turn it up and get certified  click here
 

